\label{lemma-constructible-stable-specialization-closed}
Let $R$ be a ring. Let $E \subset \Spec(R)$ be a constructible subset.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $E$ is stable under specialization, then $E$ is closed.
\item If $E$ is stable under generalization, then $E$ is open.
\end{enumerate}

statement:
Here constructible means a finite union of sets U minus V with U,V retrocompact open in Spec R; equivalently finite Boolean combinations of quasi-compact opens. Let $R$ be a ring. Let $E \subset \Spec(R)$ be a constructible subset.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $E$ is stable under specialization, then $E$ is closed.
\item If $E$ is stable under generalization, then $E$ is open.
\end{enumerate}

